## LAW 3: ZOD VALIDATION GATE

### The Rule
- ALL documents written to Firestore via seed scripts MUST be validated through a **Zod schema BEFORE** any `batch.set()` call.
- Invalid documents MUST throw an error and halt execution — NEVER silently write bad data.
- The Zod schema MUST be the single source of truth, also imported in the client `src/` types.

### Canonical Pattern (REQUIRED)
```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

const ProductSchema = z.object({
    id: z.string().min(1),
    title: z.string().min(1),
    price: z.number().positive(),
    active: z.boolean(),
    updatedAt: z.any().optional(), // Firestore Timestamp added at write time
});

type Product = z.infer<typeof ProductSchema>;

const PRODUCTS: Omit<Product, 'updatedAt'>[] = [
    { id: 'pkg-single', title: 'One-on-One', price: 89, active: true },
];

// Validate BEFORE writing
const validated = PRODUCTS.map((p, i) => {
    const result = ProductSchema.omit({ updatedAt: true }).safeParse(p);
    if (!result.success) {
        throw new Error(`Product[${i}] validation failed: ${result.error.message}`);
    }
    return result.data;
});
```

