## LAW 10: FLEET-WIDE AUDIT — `dv scan-seeds`

### The Rule
- `dv scan-seeds` MUST be run before any release involving a product catalog change.
- It scans ALL projects under `~/Developer` for seeding violations and produces a consolidated report.
- Violations are grouped by severity: 🔴 Critical (blocks deploy), 🟠 High (must fix this sprint), 🟡 Warning (tracked).

```bash
dv scan-seeds          # Audit all known Infinity Protocol projects for seeding violations
dv scan-seeds --fix    # Attempt automatic fixes (replaces hardcoded projectId, adds merge:true)
```

### What `dv scan-seeds` Checks
| Check | Detection Pattern | Severity |
|---|---|---|
| Client SDK in seed scripts | `from 'firebase/firestore'` in `scripts/seed*` | 🔴 Critical |
| Hardcoded `projectId` in `initializeApp` | `initializeApp({ projectId:` in `scripts/` | 🔴 Critical |
| Missing `{ merge: true }` in batch.set | `batch.set(` without `merge: true` | 🟠 High |
| Unguarded HTTP seed endpoints | `onRequest` + `seed` in same file, no `defineSecret` | 🔴 Critical |
| Sequential `await .set()` in loop | `await db.collection` inside `for (` loops | 🟠 High |
| No `_seedMeta` version checkpoint | Absence of `_seedMeta` in seed script | 🟡 Warning |
| Missing Zod import in seed files | No `from 'zod'` in `scripts/seed*` | 🟠 High |
| Stripe price in cents in Firestore | `price: ` integer > 10000 in product data | 🟡 Warning |

