## LAW 11: EMULATOR-FIRST LOCAL DEVELOPMENT

### The Rule
- EVERY project MUST have a `firebase.json` with `emulators` configured for Firestore (port 8080) and Auth (port 9099).
- The `npm run seed:local` script MUST target the emulator via `FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=localhost:8080`.
- NEVER run `npm run seed` (production) locally without explicitly confirming the target project via `gcloud config get-value project`.
- The `scripts/dv` utility's `dv seed --local` flag routes ALL writes to the emulator.

### Canonical Package.json Scripts (REQUIRED)
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "seed": "GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=./service-account.json npx tsx scripts/seed-products.ts",
    "seed:local": "FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=localhost:8080 npx tsx scripts/seed-products.ts",
    "seed:dry": "npx tsx scripts/seed-products.ts --dry-run",
    "seed:force": "GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=./service-account.json npx tsx scripts/seed-products.ts --force",
    "emulators": "firebase emulators:start --import=./.firebase/emulator-data --export-on-exit",
    "emulators:seed": "npm run emulators & sleep 4 && npm run seed:local"
  }
}
```

### `firebase.json` Emulator Block (REQUIRED)
```json
{
  "emulators": {
    "auth": { "port": 9099 },
    "firestore": { "port": 8080 },
    "functions": { "port": 5001 },
    "hosting": { "port": 5000 },
    "ui": { "enabled": true, "port": 4000 },
    "singleProjectMode": true
  }
}
```

