## LAW 13: EXTERNAL DATA SOURCE SEEDING

### The Rule
- When seeding from **external sources** (JSON files, CSV exports, CMS APIs, SAGE catalogs), the raw data MUST NEVER be written directly to Firestore.
- A **transform function** MUST convert the raw shape to the canonical Firestore schema BEFORE Zod validation.
- Type coercion (`z.coerce.number()`, `z.coerce.boolean()`) MUST be used for fields that may be strings in the raw source.
- External images/asset URLs MUST be validated as reachable (in dry-run mode) or stored as-is with a `pendingValidation: true` flag.
- Large external datasets (N > 500) MUST use Firestore `BulkWriter` with `.onWriteError()` handler instead of raw batch.

### Canonical Pattern — External Source → Firestore
```typescript
// §1: Raw external schema (what comes from the JSON/API)
const RawSageItemSchema = z.object({
    itemNum: z.string(),
    name: z.string(),
    prices: z.array(z.coerce.number()).optional().default([]), // coerce: '0.15' → 0.15
    quantities: z.array(z.coerce.number()).optional().default([]),
    cat1Name: z.string().optional().default(''),
});

// §2: Canonical Firestore schema (what gets written)
const FirestoreProductSchema = z.object({
    id: z.string(), // sage_{itemNum}
    title: z.string(),
    categoryId: z.enum(['printed', 'decorator', 'fulfillment', 'office', 'signs']),
    price: z.number().nonnegative(),
    isActive: z.boolean(),
});

// §3: Transform function — raw → canonical (REQUIRED separation of concerns)
function transform(raw: z.infer<typeof RawSageItemSchema>): z.infer<typeof FirestoreProductSchema> {
    return {
        id: `sage_${raw.itemNum}`,
        title: raw.name,
        categoryId: resolveCategory(raw),
        price: raw.prices[0] ?? 0,
        isActive: true,
    };
}

// §4: For large datasets — use BulkWriter instead of batch
async function bulkWrite(db: admin.firestore.Firestore, products: z.infer<typeof FirestoreProductSchema>[]) {
    const writer = db.bulkWriter();
    writer.onWriteError(error => {
        if (error.failedAttempts < 3) { return true; } // Retry up to 3x
        console.error(`[BULK WRITE ERROR] ${error.documentRef.path}: ${error.message}`);
        return false; // Give up after 3 attempts
    });

    for (const p of products) {
        const ref = db.collection('products').doc(p.id);
        writer.set(ref, { ...p, updatedAt: admin.firestore.FieldValue.serverTimestamp() }, { merge: true });
    }

    await writer.close();
    console.log(`✅ BulkWriter complete — ${products.length} documents written.`);
}
```

