## LAW 14: FIRESTORE SECURITY RULES SOVEREIGNTY

### The Problem — Rules Drift Kills Production Security
The **deployed** Firestore rules (in the Firebase console/MCP) WILL diverge from the **local** `firestore.rules` file over time. Developers hotfix rules directly in the Firebase console. The local file falls behind. When anyone then runs `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules`, they **silently downgrade production security** to match whatever is in the weaker local file.

**This is the most dangerous form of configuration drift.** It is invisible, immediate, and irreversible without a recovery plan.

### The Rules — Mandatory Pre-Deploy Protocol
1. **`dv rules:lock`** writes `.firestore-rules.lock` containing the SHA-256 hash of the current local `firestore.rules`. This file MUST be committed to version control immediately after any rules change.
2. **`dv rules:status`** computes the local rules hash and compares it to `.firestore-rules.lock`. It also scans for critical security defects. Run this before EVERY deploy.
3. If the local rules hash does NOT match the lock file, the deploy MUST be blocked until manually reviewed and re-locked.
4. **`dv rules:pull`** fetches the deployed rules via Firebase CLI and overwrites local — use to re-sync when behind the deployed version.
5. **`dv rules:validate`** runs a local static analysis scan for security defects without hitting Firebase.
6. **The production console rules = source of truth**. Never let a stale local file overwrite them.

### Required Security Standards — Every `firestore.rules` MUST Include

| Security Requirement | Pattern | Severity if Missing |
|---|---|---|
| Catch-all deny | `match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if false; }` | 🔴 Critical |
| Multi-factor `isAdmin()` | Checks custom claim AND role doc | 🔴 Critical |
| `_seedMeta` admin-only | `allow read, write: if isAdmin()` | 🔴 Critical |
| No open `allow read, write: if true` | Any collection | 🔴 Critical |
| Role escalation protection on `/users` | `.diff().affectedKeys().hasAny(['role'])` | 🔴 Critical |
| `products` admin-write-only | `allow write: if isAdmin()` | 🟠 High |
| Audit logs write-locked | `allow write: if false` (server-generated) | 🟠 High |

### CLI Commands
```bash
dv rules:status            # Compare local vs lock + security scan
dv rules:lock              # Write SHA-256 of current firestore.rules to .firestore-rules.lock
dv rules:pull              # Fetch deployed rules → overwrite local (SAFE: gets the better rules)
dv rules:validate          # Static security scan: catch-all, isAdmin, open collections
dv rules:validate --strict # Treats all HIGH findings as CRITICAL (CI mode)
```

### Canonical Hardened `firestore.rules` (Use as Minimum Baseline)
```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // ── HELPER FUNCTIONS ────────────────────────────────
    function isAuthenticated() { return request.auth != null; }
    function isOwner(userId) { return request.auth.uid == userId; }

    // Multi-factor admin: custom claim OR role doc (NEVER single-point)
    function isAdmin() {
      return isAuthenticated() && (
        request.auth.token.admin == true ||
        request.auth.token.role == 'admin' ||
        (exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)) &&
         get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)).data.role == 'admin')
      );
    }

    // ── DATA SOVEREIGNTY (admin-only, system-generated) ─
    match /_seedMeta/{docId}             { allow read: if isAdmin(); allow write: if false; }
    match /_seedSnapshots/{p=**}          { allow read, write: if false; }

    // ── PRODUCTS (public read, admin write) ─────────────
    match /products/{productId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if isAdmin();
    }

    // ── ORDERS (immutable ledger) ────────────────────────
    match /orders/{orderId} {
      allow get: if true;
      allow list: if isAdmin() || (isAuthenticated() && resource.data.userId == request.auth.uid);
      allow create: if true;
      allow update, delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // ── USERS (no role escalation) ───────────────────────
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read: if isAuthenticated() && (isOwner(userId) || isAdmin());
      allow create: if isAuthenticated() && isOwner(userId) &&
        (request.resource.data.role == 'user' || !('role' in request.resource.data));
      allow update: if isAuthenticated() &&
        ((isOwner(userId) && !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['role'])) || isAdmin());
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // ── CARTS (owner-only) ───────────────────────────────
    match /carts/{cartId} {
      allow read:           if isAdmin() || (isAuthenticated() && request.auth.uid == cartId);
      allow create, update: if isAuthenticated() && request.auth.uid == cartId;
      allow delete:         if isAdmin() || (isAuthenticated() && request.auth.uid == cartId);
    }

    // ── PUBLIC SUBMISSIONS (write-once) ──────────────────
    match /contacts/{id}    { allow create: if true; allow read, update, delete: if isAdmin(); }
    match /leads/{id}       { allow create: if true; allow read, delete: if isAdmin(); }
    match /subscribers/{id} { allow create: if true; allow read, update, delete: if isAdmin(); }

    // ── CONTENT (public read, admin write) ───────────────
    match /content/{id}    { allow read: if true; allow write: if isAdmin(); }
    match /blog_posts/{id} { allow read: if true; allow write: if isAdmin(); }

    // ── AUDIT LOGS (read admin, write system-only) ───────
    match /audit_logs/{id} { allow read: if isAdmin(); allow write: if false; }

    // ── ADMIN-ONLY COLLECTIONS ───────────────────────────
    match /subscriptions/{id} { allow read, write: if isAdmin(); }
    match /integrations/{id}  { allow read, write: if isAdmin(); }

    // ── CATCH-ALL DENY ── REQUIRED — NEVER REMOVE ────────
    // New collections are LOCKED until explicitly allowed above.
    match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if false; }
  }
}
```

### CI Integration — Rules Lock Check (Add to `templates/ci-test.yml`)
```yaml
- name: Verify Firestore Rules Lock (Law 14 — Data Sovereignty v8.4.0)
  run: |
    if [ ! -f ".firestore-rules.lock" ]; then
      echo "[RULES LOCK] ERROR: .firestore-rules.lock is missing!"
      echo "Run: dv rules:lock — to generate it, then commit the lock file."
      exit 1
    fi
    LOCAL_SHA=$(shasum -a 256 firestore.rules | awk '{print $1}')
    LOCK_SHA=$(cat .firestore-rules.lock)
    if [ "$LOCAL_SHA" != "$LOCK_SHA" ]; then
      echo "[RULES DRIFT] firestore.rules changed since last lock!"
      echo "  Lock SHA:  $LOCK_SHA"
      echo "  Local SHA: $LOCAL_SHA"
      echo "Run 'dv rules:status' to review. If safe, run 'dv rules:lock' and commit."
      exit 1
    fi
    echo "[RULES LOCK] ✅ Verified. Rules match lock file."
```


